+# Diagnostic evidence input review
+
+Completed on 14 October 2026 by Codex (automated). Application version: 0.4.4.
+
+## Preserved and tested ZIP
+
+`GridSense_Release_Prepared.zip` was preserved before this work. Its SHA-256
+is `533893def3ddce2f50219f7634da524545f13fddca33bd3282041778419c6e46`.
+All 420 manifest files and ZIP CRCs checked successfully. Extracted source in
+a path containing spaces and Unicode loaded its own Python module, reran the
+four native diagnostic controls and strictly replayed the bundled regression.
+Installed locked dependencies were reused.
+[Extracted-package record](verification/evidence-input-2026-10-14/extracted-followup-package.json).
+
+The preceding 284-backend/38-browser full verification remains under
+[follow-up checkpoint checks](verification/followup-2026-10-14/checkpoint-checks/verification.json).
+The previous diagnostic results are also retained as
+[historical results](verification/evidence-input-2026-10-14/reference-sensitivity-before.json).
+
+## Reproduced defect and fix
+
+The diagnostic verifier accepted an altered measurement containing
+`Infinity` as equal to the finite native result. Its relative comparator
+assumes finite numbers: with an infinite operand both sides of its relative
+allowance test can become infinite. Python's JSON reader accepts non-standard
+Infinity/NaN tokens and can overflow a numeric literal such as `1e999`.
+
+An actual command execution from the extracted saved source returned exit 0
+for an Infinity-altered report. The corrected source returns exit 2 with a
+non-finite-data error and no traceback.
+[Before/after reproduction](verification/evidence-input-2026-10-14/nonfinite-reproduction.json).
+
+The diagnostic checker now requires finite JSON data before comparing
+saved and actual reports. The CLI validates the input before starting the
+study and reports invalid file/object/comparison data as argument errors.
+Ten added regressions cover positive/negative infinity and NaN in measurements,
+infinite tolerances/residuals, and all three non-standard tokens plus positive
+and negative numeric overflow through real CLI executions. All 14 diagnostic
+regression cases pass.
+
+This fix changes the diagnostic runner and its tests. The 37 production
+module/model files retain the saved ZIP's bytes. Simulation, core replay,
+model inputs, frozen reference targets and acceptance tolerances are unchanged.
+The recorded source digest for the updated diagnostic is regenerated through
+an actual native study execution. The four configurations still give 52/56,
+53/56, 56/56 and 56/56; native defaults remain the original primary result.
+[Diagnostic scope](REFERENCE_SENSITIVITY.md).
+
+## Verification and delivery
+
+Complete Linux verification passes 294 backend and 38 browser tests with no
+failures, skips, errors or flaky cases. The 29 runner steps comprise 28 passes
+and the explicitly retained original electrical-reference mismatch. Native
+backend/frontend HTTP, six workflow replays, desktop/phone geometry checks
+and abrupt-restart recovery pass. Existing dependencies and compatible
+Chromium are reused; source/build fingerprints are checked by release tooling.
+[Latest verification](VERIFICATION.md),
+[complete current report](verification/checks/verification.json).
+
+The ZIP includes the corrected runner, regenerated diagnostic data, the
+new integrity/extraction records and retained earlier evidence. An
+[incremental source patch](reviews/evidence-input-2026-10-14.patch) applies
+to `GridSense_Release_Prepared.zip`. Verification evidence is supplied in the
+complete ZIP; rerun verification after applying a source patch.
+
+GitHub is available but not enabled here, and the local repository has no
+remote destination. Repository publication and hosted CI therefore remain
+pending a connected GitHub integration and repository URL. Windows execution,
+independent reviews and the owner's project license selection remain open.
+No remote repository was created or published.
